  "IMF-22c": { type: "support", doc: "imf", page: 22, relatedLead: ["IMF-12c"], text: "Where we've been, where we're going\nWe pioneered PCR testing and brought it from the back office to the front lines, along with more automation, efficiency and simplification. And we’ll continue to shine a light on newer innovations (like Mass Spectrometry and TAGS multiplexing examples) to ensure patients, practitioners and researchers have access to our most powerful solutions.", source: "Inspiring visibility messages — Where we've been, where we're going" },
  "IMF-22d": { type: "proof", doc: "imf", page: 22, relatedLead: ["IMF-12c"], text: "Inventing sequencing by expansion: a DNA sequencing breakthrough\nAfter countless experiments and nearly 10 years of work, Roche unveils its new “SBX” (sequencing by expansion) technology that has the potential to revolutionise the way DNA is sequenced.", source: "Inspiring visibility messages — Inventing sequencing by expansion" },
  "IMF-22e": { type: "support", doc: "imf", page: 22, relatedLead: ["IMF-12c"], text: "See the unseen\nSome of our most powerful innovations—from AI to machine learning to interconnected digital systems, some within Roche and some as collaborations with partners—don’t get a lot of time in the spotlight, but they have the power to truly improve patient outcomes.", source: "Inspiring visibility messages — See the unseen" },
  "IMF-22f": { type: "proof", doc: "imf", page: 22, relatedLead: ["IMF-12c"], text: "Addressing unmet patient needs in burdensome diseases\nIn 2024, Roche was granted FDA Breakthrough Device Designations for two blood-based tests that represent significant advancements in disease areas with growing societal burden. One test is the Tina-quant Lp(a) assay, which measures a critical marker for people at risk of cardiovascular disease who could benefit from targeted therapy. The other test is the Elecsys pTau217 plasma assay, which identifies the presence or absence of amyloid pathology, a pathological feature of Alzheimer’s disease.", source: "Inspiring visibility messages — Addressing unmet patient needs" },
  "IMF-23a": { type: "proof", doc: "imf", page: 23, relatedLead: ["IMF-12b"], text: "Our significant focus in R&D makes all the difference\n13B CHF R&D investment in 2024\n327 Active in-licensing agreements\n133 Active out-licensing agreements", source: "Our significant focus in R&D makes all the difference" },
  "IMF-25a": { type: "lead", doc: "imf", page: 25, text: "We are innovators. Evidence-based detectives. And unrelenting truth-seekers.\n\nRoche Diagnostics has been at the forefront of scientific breakthroughs for the past century, quietly pushing healthcare forward and improving processes for scientists, practitioners and patients alike.\n\nOur collaborative digital ecosystem allows us to connect different areas of expertise throughout Roche to leverage diagnostic data and discover hidden answers to healthcare’s biggest questions.\n\nFrom mass spectrometry innovation to the continued evolution of legacy PCR testing to collaborative research across all areas of clinical chemistry, immunochemistry, pathology lab developments, digital health solutions, next generation systems and more, Roche Diagnostics is, and always will be, ahead of care.", source: "Campaign story", buyingInfluence: ["clinical", "financial", "operational"], customerChallenge: ["access-to-innovation"] },
  "IMF-30a": { type: "lead", doc: "imf", page: 30, text: "next generation technologies — Getting to precision with more speed and less hands-on time via molecular and sequencing automation", source: "Headline + subhead library", buyingInfluence: ["operational"], customerChallenge: ["automation-digitalization"] },
